    title: "Microsoft 為 Linux 7.4 推出 Para-Virtualized IOMMU 驅動，強化 Hyper-V 虛擬機的設備隔離與 DMA 保護",
    summary: "Microsoft 為其 Hyper-V 虛擬化平台，為 Linux 7.4 核心週期貢獻了一款新的 Para-Virtualized IOMMU 驅動（名稱為 \"hv-iommu-guest\"）。此驅動透過新的 HYPERV_PVIOMMU Kconfig 選項啟用，旨在提升在 Hyper-V 上運行的 Linux 客體機（guest VMs）的安全性與設備支援。它能為分配給客體機的設備提供內核層級的 DMA 保護，並支援透過 VFIO 等方式將設備分配給使用者空間。此功能適用於支援 Intel VT-d 和 AMD IOMMU 的系統。開發者已使用 NVMe 設備和 Intel DSA 加速器設備進行驗證。此功能自 2023 年 12 月提出 RFC 補丁以來已醞釀良久，預計在 Linux 7.4 穩定版發布時納入。",
    tags: ["Microsoft", "Hyper-V", "Linux 7.4", "IOMMU", "Para-virtualized", "DMA", "VFIO"],
    title_en: "Microsoft Releases Para-Virtualized IOMMU Driver for Linux 7.4, Enhancing Hyper-V VM Device Isolation and DMA Protection",
    summary_en: "Microsoft has contributed a new Para-Virtualized IOMMU driver (named \"hv-iommu-guest\") for its Hyper-V virtualization platform, targeting the Linux 7.4 kernel cycle. This driver is enabled via the new HYPERV_PVIOMMU Kconfig option and aims to enhance the security and device support for Linux guest VMs running on Hyper-V. It provides kernel-level DMA protection for devices assigned to the guest VMs and supports device assignment to user space via methods like VFIO. This feature is applicable to systems supporting Intel VT-d and AMD IOMMU. Developers have validated this feature using NVMe devices and Intel DSA accelerator devices. This functionality, which was first proposed via an RFC patch in December 2023, has been in development for some time and is expected to be included in the Linux 7.4 stable release.",
