    category: "Windows",
    title: "Microsoft 承認 Windows 11 設計無法滿足所有用戶，強調個性化與多樣化工作流",
    summary: "本文討論了 Microsoft 在 Windows 11 進行「UI 再造」（UI rejuvenation）的設計挑戰。Windows 設計副總裁 Diego Baca 指出，為超過十億用戶設計作業系統最大的挑戰在於「每個人都有不同的偏好和工作流程」。Microsoft 近期推出了新的 Windows Search 功能，允許用戶直接在搜尋中執行設定變更，取代傳統的設定介面。然而，這也引發了關於是否應移除 Start Menu 的討論。此外，Microsoft 曾推動 Start Menu 的「推薦」（Recommendations）功能，旨在根據用戶的上下文和習慣來預測和展示文件或應用程式，例如「昨日錯過的會議錄影」或「下午兩點常使用的應用程式」。儘管 Microsoft 聲稱這些功能是基於用戶回饋，但文章指出，這可能只是公司研究人員選擇性地採用了部分意見，忽略了大多數用戶的真實需求。總體而言，Microsoft 承諾在 2026 年重點進行 Windows 11 的設計更新，目標是提供更多 WinUI 基礎的現代化功能和更高的客製化選項。",
    tags: ["Windows 11", "Microsoft", "UI/UX", "Start Menu", "Windows Search", "Diego Baca"],
    title_en: "Microsoft Acknowledges Windows 11 Design Cannot Satisfy All Users, Emphasizes Personalization and Diverse Workflows",
    summary_en: "This article discusses the design challenges Microsoft faces with Windows 11's 'UI rejuvenation.' Windows Design Vice President Diego Baca pointed out that the biggest challenge in designing an operating system for over a billion users is that 'everyone has different preferences and workflows.' Microsoft recently introduced a new Windows Search feature that allows users to make settings changes directly within the search function, replacing the traditional settings interface. However, this has also sparked a debate about whether the Start Menu should be removed. Furthermore, Microsoft previously promoted the Start Menu's 'Recommendations' feature, which aims to predict and display documents or applications based on the user's context and habits, such as 'missed meeting recordings from yesterday' or 'applications commonly used at 2 PM.' Although Microsoft claims these features are based on user feedback, the article suggests that this may merely be the company's researchers selectively adopting certain opinions while ignoring the genuine needs of the majority of users. Overall, Microsoft has committed to focusing on Windows 11 design updates in 2026, aiming to provide more WinUI-based modernization features and higher customization options.",
