    title: "AI系統具備執行工業控制系統（OT）惡意攻擊的能力，威脅水電等基礎設施",
    summary: "根據 Booz Allen Hamilton 的報告，自主 AI 系統已展現出執行「惡夢級」網路攻擊的完整能力，能夠針對關鍵的營運技術（OT）和工業設備進行攻擊，從而癱瘓水、電等日常必需的基礎設施。測試結果顯示，AI 模型能在極短時間內（例如 16 分鐘內）從周邊網路入侵擴展到工業控制網路內部，並具備高精度的工程級操作能力。這些模型能夠識別關鍵資產、尋找漏洞、並將漏洞轉化為實際的入侵路徑，甚至能操控 PLC、SCADA 平台、變頻驅動器（VFD）和機械手臂。報告指出，這意味著攻擊者不再需要具備深厚的 OT 專業知識，只需利用 AI 代理即可造成實體破壞。此外，許多 OT 設備缺乏認證或加密機制，使得惡意指令的執行變得更容易。建議業界應加強 OT 網路的基礎資安實踐，並進行更多模擬測試，以應對 AI 帶來的巨大風險。",
    tags: ["AI 攻擊", "OT 網路", "SCADA", "工業控制系統", "Booz Allen Hamilton", "基礎設施安全"],
    title_en: "AI Systems Possess Capability to Execute Industrial Control System (OT) Malicious Attacks, Threatening Water and Power Infrastructure",
    summary_en: "According to a report by Booz Allen Hamilton, autonomous AI systems have demonstrated the full capability to execute \"nightmare-level\" cyberattacks. These systems can target critical Operational Technology (OT) and industrial equipment, potentially paralyzing essential infrastructure such as water and power. Test results showed that AI models can expand from peripheral network intrusions to within the industrial control network in a very short time (e.g., within 16 minutes), possessing high-precision, engineering-grade operational capabilities. These models can identify critical assets, locate vulnerabilities, and translate those vulnerabilities into actual intrusion paths, even controlling PLCs, SCADA platforms, Variable Frequency Drives (VFDs), and robotic arms. The report suggests that this means attackers no longer need deep OT expertise, only utilizing AI agents to cause physical damage. Furthermore, many OT devices lack certification or encryption mechanisms, making the execution of malicious commands easier. The industry is advised to strengthen foundational cybersecurity practices for OT networks and conduct more simulation testing to address the immense risks posed by AI.",
