    title: "HPE高階主管預測AI將接管網路維護，主張「自駕網路」將取代人工故障排除",
    summary: "HPE網路業務總經理Rami Rahim推動HPE的「自駕網路」（self-driving networks）概念，這屬於AIOps（AI-assisted monitoring and automated remediation）範疇。Rahim主張，AI輔助的網路監控與自動修復技術，將使人工網路管理員逐漸退出故障排除的場域。他預測，在兩到三年內，幾乎所有需要人工介入的網路問題都將被AI解決。他指出，目前企業最常見的故障票單是「Wi-Fi不佳」，AI能比人類更快地找出問題並透過代理（agents）進行修復。隨著企業內部工作代理（agents）數量遠超人力，對可靠網路的需求將持續增長，使得AI成為管理複雜網路的唯一可行方案。HPE透過整合Juniper Networks的技術，將這項自駕網路技術應用於其整個混合雲產品組合，並已將網路結構管理能力整合至OpsRamp等可觀察性軟體中。",
    tags: ["HPE", "Juniper Networks", "AIOps", "自駕網路", "網路自動化", "混合雲"],
    title_en: "HPE Senior Executive Predicts AI Will Take Over Network Maintenance, Claiming 'Self-Driving Networks' Will Replace Manual Troubleshooting",
    summary_en: "HPE Network Business General Manager Rami Rahim is promoting HPE's 'self-driving networks' concept, which falls under the scope of AIOps (AI-assisted monitoring and automated remediation). Rahim argues that AI-assisted network monitoring and automated remediation technologies will gradually render human network administrators obsolete in the field of troubleshooting. He predicts that within two to three years, nearly all network issues requiring human intervention will be solved by AI. He points out that the most common corporate trouble ticket currently is 'poor Wi-Fi,' which AI can identify and fix faster than humans using agents. As the number of internal corporate agents far exceeds human capacity, the demand for reliable networks will continue to grow, making AI the only viable solution for managing complex networks. HPE is applying this self-driving network technology across its entire hybrid cloud portfolio by integrating Juniper Networks' technology, and has already integrated network structure management capabilities into observability software such as OpsRamp.",
