    title: "研究人員開發新技術：控制 2D 半導體晶體生長，推動下一代晶片製造",
    summary: "根據發表在《Nature》上的研究，科學家提出了一種新的方法，能夠精確控制二維（2D）半導體晶體的生長位置。這項技術透過使用「蝕刻通量」（etching flux）來抑制晶體在特定圖案區域內除了幾何中心以外任何地方的形成，從而解決了傳統 2D 材料晶體隨機生長、導致電性能下降和器件不均勻的問題。研究團隊利用此「蝕刻通量介導單中心成核」（EF-SCN）過程，成功製造出工作電場效應電晶體（FETs），並報告了比先前報導的 MoS₂ 電晶體更高的電荷載子遷移率。在一個兩公分基板的測試中，該過程在 400 個圖案位點中達到了 397 個單晶體，晶圓良率高達 99.3%。這項技術對於堆疊 2D 半導體器件到矽晶片至關重要，有助於將邏輯與記憶體更緊密地整合，並為實現 CFETs（互補電場效應電晶體）等 3D 堆疊架構提供了基礎。相關公司 TDS Innovation 預計此類 2D 半導體在 2030 年左右可實現商業應用。",
    tags: ["2D 半導體", "MoS₂", "晶片製造", "FETs", "CFETs", "Nature"],
    title_en: "Researchers Develop New Technique: Controlling 2D Semiconductor Crystal Growth to Drive Next-Generation Chip Manufacturing",
    summary_en: "According to research published in *Nature*, scientists have proposed a novel method to precisely control the growth location of two-dimensional (2D) semiconductor crystals. This technique utilizes an “etching flux” to suppress crystal formation anywhere within a specific patterned area, except for the geometric center. This addresses the issue of random crystal growth in traditional 2D materials, which typically leads to degraded electrical performance and device non-uniformity. The research team employed this “etching flux-mediated single crystal nucleation” (EF-SCN) process, successfully fabricating field-effect transistors (FETs) and reporting a higher charge carrier mobility in MoS₂ transistors compared to previously reported values. In a test on a two-inch substrate, the process achieved 397 single crystals out of 400 patterned sites, resulting in a wafer yield of 99.3%. This technology is crucial for stacking 2D semiconductor devices onto silicon wafers, helping to integrate logic and memory more closely, and providing a foundation for 3D stacked architectures such as Complementary FETs (CFETs). Related company TDS Innovation anticipates that such 2D semiconductors could achieve commercial application around 2030.",
